# Generated project inventory output
inventory_output.txt

# The extracted conversation corpus.
#
# research/codex-history/raw/ holds the owner's personal conversation text.
# It is regenerated from the local Codex store by
# tools/extract_codex_history.py, so it is output, not source, and it is
# not published to a public repository. The registry beside it - the
# index, the thread metadata and the digest - is the part the build
# actually uses, and that is committed.
research/codex-history/raw/

# The text-document inventory is a generated index over the owner's
# documents. It is committed because it is the coverage record; the
# documents it describes are not.

# Research artefacts: downloaded model weights and generated numeric
# outputs. These are data the build produces or fetches, not source.
# They stay on disk for the research scripts, which read them locally,
# and they are kept out of the repository so a push is a push and not a
# two-gigabyte transfer.
research/lm-compression/gpt-neo-125M-fp32/
research/lm-compression/packed-int2.bin
research/lm-compression/packed-int4.bin
research/build81/fea/fea_m3.dat
research/build84/storage/
research/build85/pattern/storage/

# The conversation digests are derived from the raw corpus.
research/codex-history/digests/

# The recovered conversation corpus.
#
# The owner's own conversations are not published in bulk. The digests
# beside them are, because a digest is the rollup: what the corpus says,
# counted and grouped, rather than the text itself. The same rule applies
# here as to the Codex history: the raw material stays on disk, the
# abstraction is what the build uses.
research/conversation-corpus/index.json
research/external-chats/
research/chatgpt-all-conversations.json

# The statements the owner made about each project, in bulk. The readable
# rollup beside it is published, because it is what a person reads; the
# index is the machine form of the same quotes.
research/conversations/project-conversations.json

# The README cache from the repository analysis. Six hundred READMEs from
# other people's repositories are third-party text and are not published;
# the analysis derived from them is.
research/github-repos/.readme-cache/

# The absorbed projects.
#
# Each of these keeps its own repository and its own GitHub remote, and
# each is a project of its own with its own build manifest. The parent
# project must not track them: a nested repository is not part of the
# parent's history, and tracking it would put a second project's
# contents into this one's commits.
absorbed/self-building-ai/
apps/Athena/
apps/Decentralized Messaging App/
apps/Food Wiki App/
apps/IDE-Workspace/
apps/LedgerLands/
apps/Multi-Cross-Platform-Trading-Bot/
apps/Poietek/
apps/aetherion-engine/
apps/aetherius-health-library/
apps/football-card-game/
apps/quantum-ai-assistant/
apps/sovereign-financial-os/
books/Architecture of Shadows Book/
ecosystem/Niche_platform/
ecosystem/Web-platform/
ecosystem/aetherial-platform/
ecosystem/crossplatform---multiplatform/
kernel/Genesis/
predecessors/QVA-merged/
predecessors/Quantum-OS/
predecessors/Veyra/
predecessors/aetherial/
predecessors/aetherium/
predecessors/aetherius-os-prototype/
predecessors/aetherius-os-worldclass-prototype/
predecessors/ai-digital-clone/
predecessors/holonav-os/
tools/Hermes-Config-Audit/

# First-party slices that do NOT have a repository of their own.
#
# The block above assumes every ignored directory is a nested git
# repository with its own remote. That is true for Poietek, IDE-Workspace,
# LedgerLands, the football card game, aetherion-engine, the book, the
# predecessors with .git directories and the ecosystem repositories. It is
# not true for the slices below: they are part of Aetherius-OS, they are
# run by apps/verify.mjs, and leaving them ignored meant their source and
# tests could never be committed or reviewed. These negations re-include
# only those slices.
!apps/Athena/
!apps/Athena/**
!apps/Decentralized Messaging App/
!apps/Decentralized Messaging App/**
!apps/aetherius-health-library/
!apps/aetherius-health-library/**
# The two frequency lists are the data the health-library tests read. The
# Rife handbook introduction and the OCR note are reference material whose
# redistribution rights are not established, so they stay local-only.
apps/aetherius-health-library/RifeHandbook5thEdIntroduction.txt
apps/aetherius-health-library/Healing_Web_OCR_first2.txt
!apps/quantum-ai-assistant/
!apps/quantum-ai-assistant/**
!apps/sovereign-financial-os/
!apps/sovereign-financial-os/**
!predecessors/holonav-os/
!predecessors/holonav-os/**
!predecessors/aetherius-os-prototype/
!predecessors/aetherius-os-prototype/**
!predecessors/aetherius-os-worldclass-prototype/
!predecessors/aetherius-os-worldclass-prototype/**
